WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.697 --> 00:00:19.079
night Friar Tuck feasted and sang with Robin and his men.

2
00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:25.741
Robin told Alan of Dale's sad story to the friar, and then explained his own plan.

3
00:00:25.761 --> 00:00:31.524
"My plan can work, but I need your help with something," added Robin.

4
00:00:33.808 --> 00:00:35.509
Friar Tuck didn't hesitate.

5
00:00:35.529 --> 00:00:38.071
"I can do it," he agreed.

6
00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:40.393
"I'll marry Alan and Ellen."

7
00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:42.274
"Good!" said Robin.

8
00:00:44.275 --> 00:00:47.257
The next morning was Ellen's wedding to Sir Stephen.

9
00:00:47.918 --> 00:00:53.682
Robin surprised his men by dressing in bright, striped clothes and carrying a harp.

10
00:00:54.982 --> 00:00:57.724
"Look!" said Little John, pointing at Robin.

11
00:00:57.744 --> 00:00:59.946
"It's a colorful bird!"

12
00:01:00.686 --> 00:01:02.307
The men roared with laughter.

13
00:01:04.192 --> 00:01:05.573
Robin was laughing too.

14
00:01:05.593 --> 00:01:09.956
"This is my disguise for Alan's wedding," he explained.

15
00:01:09.976 --> 00:01:11.336
"I'm a minstrel.

16
00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:14.338
Carry these two bags of gold for me, Little John."

17
00:01:15.439 --> 00:01:18.801
Robin set off for the church with Alan and twenty other men.

18
00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:22.603
When they arrived, they hid outside behind a wall.

19
00:01:23.463 --> 00:01:26.625
They were waiting for someone to come to unlock the church door.

20
00:01:27.806 --> 00:01:30.007
At last an old friar appeared.

21
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.602
As he struggled with some keys, Friar Tuck stepped up to help him.

22
00:01:35.622 --> 00:01:40.404
"I hear there's a wedding today," said Friar Tuck.

23
00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:42.485
"I'd like to see that."

24
00:01:42.505 --> 00:01:47.168
"You're welcome to stay for the wedding," said the old friar.

25
00:01:48.348 --> 00:01:52.130
Friar Tuck unlocked the door and the two men entered the church.

26
00:01:53.871 --> 00:01:55.852
Robin sat outside by the door.

27
00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.181
He soon spotted six men approaching on horses.

28
00:02:01.261 --> 00:02:03.762
The Bishop of Hereford was in the lead.

29
00:02:04.502 --> 00:02:09.224
His clothes were made of beautiful silk; a gold chain dangled from his neck.

30
00:02:10.684 --> 00:02:11.564
Robin frowned.

31
00:02:11.584 --> 00:02:14.645
"That bishop is dressed like a prince.

32
00:02:15.345 --> 00:02:17.346
He got his money from cheating the poor!"

33
00:02:18.606 --> 00:02:21.147
The bishop noticed Robin as he came closer.

34
00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.828
"Who are you?"

35
00:02:23.408 --> 00:02:24.128
asked the bishop.

36
00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.065
"I'm the best minstrel in England," replied Robin.

37
00:02:28.085 --> 00:02:32.307
"When I play, I'll make the bride love the groom forever."

38
00:02:33.187 --> 00:02:34.228
The bishop laughed.

39
00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:38.990
"If you can do that, I'll give you whatever you want.

40
00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.991
My cousin, Sir Stephen, is the groom."

41
00:02:43.632 --> 00:02:45.993
"We have a deal," replied Robin.

42
00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:49.434
Soon the wedding party began to arrive on horseback.

43
00:02:50.895 --> 00:02:54.116
Sir Stephen was a tall, thin man with gray hair.

44
00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.709
Beside him rode the bride's father.

45
00:02:58.889 --> 00:03:01.470
Next came the bride, Ellen, in a carriage.

46
00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.571
She was very pretty, but she looked very sad.

47
00:03:06.671 --> 00:03:08.472
Behind her rode some knights.

48
00:03:08.492 --> 00:03:13.213
"Play your harp now," the bishop said to Robin.

49
00:03:13.233 --> 00:03:17.374
"No, it's not the right time," said Robin quickly.

50
00:03:18.194 --> 00:03:21.115
He really had no idea how to play a harp!

51
00:03:22.055 --> 00:03:23.556
Everyone entered the church.

52
00:03:25.136 --> 00:03:26.497
Robin stepped forward.

53
00:03:27.438 --> 00:03:29.080
"What kind of wedding is this?"

54
00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.100
he shouted.

55
00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.482
"The groom is too old!

56
00:03:32.583 --> 00:03:35.045
And the bride is engaged to another man!"

57
00:03:37.126 --> 00:03:42.831
Robin blew his horn three times and Alan burst through the door with Robin's other men.

58
00:03:45.694 --> 00:03:47.095
Ellen's face lit up.

59
00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:50.217
"Alan!" she cried happily.

60
00:03:51.098 --> 00:03:52.960
Ellen's father was furious.

61
00:03:53.796 --> 00:03:56.499
"You're to blame for this, Alan of Dale!"

62
00:03:56.879 --> 00:03:58.921
he said with a furious scowl.

63
00:03:58.941 --> 00:04:02.044
"No, I'm to blame.

64
00:04:03.105 --> 00:04:06.588
I'm Robin Hood, and I say Ellen will marry Alan!"

65
00:04:06.608 --> 00:04:08.990
"Please, Father!"

66
00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.271
begged Ellen.

67
00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:12.773
"I'm in love with Alan."

68
00:04:12.793 --> 00:04:16.176
"You'll marry Sir Stephen or no one!"

69
00:04:16.497 --> 00:04:17.397
shouted her father.

70
00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:20.100
Sir Stephen suddenly spoke up.

71
00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.102
"I can't marry a woman who loves another man."

72
00:04:25.122 --> 00:04:30.605
He looked sadly at Ellen for a few moments and then hurried out of the church.

73
00:04:36.648 --> 00:04:39.330
Robin gave Ellen's father two bags of gold.

74
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:42.632
"Perhaps this will help to win your approval."

75
00:04:43.712 --> 00:04:45.393
Ellen's father's eyes lit up.

76
00:04:46.394 --> 00:04:50.196
"I'll give my blessing to this marriage," he said.

77
00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:52.077
Everyone cheered.

78
00:04:56.018 --> 00:04:57.259
time for the wedding!"

79
00:04:57.659 --> 00:04:58.419
cried Robin.

80
00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.061
Friar Tuck did his part and married the happy couple.

81
00:05:04.982 --> 00:05:06.322
The bishop looked worried.

82
00:05:07.603 --> 00:05:10.124
He was afraid of what Robin might do next.

83
00:05:10.144 --> 00:05:14.246
"It's time for me to go," he said quickly.

84
00:05:14.266 --> 00:05:15.726
"Wait a minute.

85
00:05:16.327 --> 00:05:19.468
You promised to give me whatever I want," said Robin.

86
00:05:20.792 --> 00:05:23.614
"But you didn't play a tune," said the bishop.

87
00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:27.477
"I only said I'd play.

88
00:05:28.177 --> 00:05:30.298
I never said I'd play a tune.

89
00:05:30.999 --> 00:05:32.920
Instead I played a trick.

90
00:05:33.681 --> 00:05:35.862
And now the bride will love her groom forever.

91
00:05:36.863 --> 00:05:39.405
Give your gold necklace to Ellen," ordered Robin.

92
00:05:40.846 --> 00:05:42.647
Grumbling, the bishop obeyed.

93
00:05:43.247 --> 00:05:45.188
He handed the necklace to the bride.

94
00:05:45.208 --> 00:05:50.152
"You should be our guest at a feast someday," Robin said to the bishop.

95
00:05:51.232 --> 00:05:52.052
"Oh no!"

96
00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:57.455
The bishop went pale and ran from the church as fast as he could.

97
00:05:59.415 --> 00:06:02.297
The happy bride and groom thanked Robin for his help.

98
00:06:03.797 --> 00:06:04.698
Robin bowed.

99
00:06:04.718 --> 00:06:06.758
"You're quite welcome."

100
00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.601
Then Robin and his men started toward home.

101
00:06:12.621 --> 00:06:15.802
"I had so much fun today!"

102
00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.043
Friar Tuck said.

103
00:06:17.063 --> 00:06:20.224
"Robin, will you let me join your band?"

104
00:06:20.989 --> 00:06:22.836
Robin grinned at Friar Tuck.

105
00:06:24.121 --> 00:06:25.687
"Of course," he said.
